# Next.js and React standards

## App Router conventions

- All routes live under `apps/web/app/`. The legacy `pages/` directory must not be used.
- Each route directory contains `page.tsx` for the route, optionally `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`.
- Route groups in parentheses, e.g. `(auth)`, `(dashboard)`, organize without affecting the URL.
- Dynamic segments use `[param]`, catch-all uses `[...slug]`.

## Server vs client components

- Default to server components. Do not add `"use client"` unless you genuinely need interactivity, browser APIs, React state, or React hooks.
- Fetch data in server components directly. Never use `useEffect` + `fetch` for data that the server can get.
- Mark `"use client"` as specifically as possible. A large `page.tsx` being server, with a small `ClientWidget` being client, is better than marking the whole page client.
- Client components can import server components as children, but not the other way around.

## Data fetching

- Server components: `async` function components that await data directly. Use try-catch for errors, let loading.tsx handle loading state.
- Client components: use TanStack Query (`@tanstack/react-query`). Never fetch in `useEffect`.
- API calls go through a central `apps/web/lib/api-client.ts` axios or fetch wrapper that handles the base URL, auth token, and error normalization.
- Never put raw `fetch` calls scattered across components.

## Components

- File name kebab-case, component name PascalCase: `document-editor.tsx` exports `DocumentEditor`.
- Props typed with an interface or type named `<ComponentName>Props`.
- Explicit return type on components is optional for plain JSX, required when the component returns something non-trivial.
- Components under 200 lines. Above that, extract subcomponents or hooks.
- No business logic in components. Extract to custom hooks (`use-*.ts`) or services.

## State management

- Local UI state: `useState`, `useReducer`.
- Cross-component state: lift up, use context, or Zustand for bigger stores.
- Server state: TanStack Query. Never duplicate server state into local state.
- Form state: React Hook Form, not local state.

## Forms

- Every form uses React Hook Form + Zod resolver (`@hookform/resolvers/zod`).
- Zod schema imported from `packages/shared-types` when the schema is shared with the backend.
- Never use uncontrolled inputs for forms that submit data.
- Submit handler is async, shows loading state while pending, shows error and success via toast.
- Disable submit button during pending state.

## UI components

- Use shadcn/ui components (`apps/web/components/ui/`). Do not build custom buttons, inputs, dialogs, cards, or tables from scratch.
- Tailwind utility classes for all styling. No custom CSS files unless absolutely necessary.
- Follow shadcn patterns: `Button` with variants, `Input` with controlled state, `Dialog` for modals.
- Icons from `lucide-react`. Do not use emoji as icons.

## Feedback and states

- Every data-fetching page has:
  - A skeleton loader via `loading.tsx` or inline skeleton components (not a raw spinner)
  - An error state via `error.tsx` or inline error with a retry button
  - An empty state with meaningful copy and a CTA, not "No data"
- Use `sonner` for toasts on action success and failure.
- Button pending states: disable the button and swap label to "Saving..." or similar.
- Form errors: inline under each field plus toast on submit failure.

## Accessibility

- All form inputs have associated labels (not just placeholders).
- Interactive elements have `aria-label` if their purpose is not clear from text content.
- Keyboard navigation works: tab order logical, escape closes modals, enter submits forms.
- Sufficient color contrast. Do not rely on color alone to convey meaning.
- Use semantic HTML: `<button>` for buttons, `<a>` for links, `<nav>` for navigation.

## Performance

- Images via `next/image`, never raw `<img>`. Provide width, height, alt.
- Dynamic imports for heavy components not needed on first paint: `const Heavy = dynamic(() => import("./heavy"))`.
- Memoize expensive computations with `useMemo`, expensive callbacks with `useCallback`, but only when there is a measured problem. Do not prematurely optimize.
- Keep client bundles small. If a library is only needed server-side, keep the import in a server component.

## Routing and navigation

- Use `Link` from `next/link` for client-side navigation, not `<a>`.
- Use `useRouter` from `next/navigation` (not `next/router`) for programmatic navigation in client components.
- Use absolute paths with the `@/` alias configured in tsconfig. Never `../../../components/foo`.

## Metadata and SEO

- Export `metadata` object from page.tsx or layout.tsx for title, description, Open Graph tags.
- Use `generateMetadata` for dynamic metadata based on route params.
- Set `robots`, `openGraph`, `twitter` as appropriate.

## Mobile responsiveness

- The patient signing page and the landing page MUST work perfectly on mobile (375px width minimum).
- Provider-facing pages (dashboard, editor) must at least not break on mobile, but can be optimized for desktop.
- Use Tailwind breakpoints consistently: `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`. Mobile-first.

## Things never do in Next.js / React

- Never `useEffect` with `fetch` for data that should come from the server
- Never `<img>` instead of `next/image`
- Never access `window` or `document` without a `typeof window !== "undefined"` guard, or better, move to a client component
- Never put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` env vars (they are exposed to the browser)
- Never import server-only code into a client component
- Never `any` as a prop type
